        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.736,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Number Play"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.401,
            0.114
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6.2 Picking Parity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.123,
            0.848,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "Kishor has some number cards and is working on a puzzle: There are 5 boxes, and each box should contain exactly 1 number card. The numbers in the boxes should sum to 30. Can you help him find a way to do it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.199,
            0.74,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.251,
            0.824,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.364,
            0.848,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "Can you figure out which 5 cards add to 30? Is it possible? There are many ways of choosing 5 cards from this collection. Is there a way to find a solution without checking all possibilities? Let us find out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.447,
            0.847,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": "？ Add a few even numbers together. What kind of number do you get? Does it matter how many numbers are added?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.497,
            0.846,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "Any even number can be arranged in pairs without any leftovers. Some even numbers are shown here, arranged in pairs."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.541,
            0.658,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.637,
            0.782,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "As we see in the figure, adding any number of even numbers will result in a number which can still be arranged in pairs without any leftovers. In other words, the sum will always be an even number."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.797,
            0.63,
            0.838,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.72,
            0.847,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": "? Now, add a few odd numbers together. What kind of number do you get? Does it matter how many odd numbers are added?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.77,
            0.848,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": "Odd numbers can not be arranged in pairs. An odd number is one more than a collection of pairs. Some odd numbers are shown below:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.822,
            0.673,
            0.91
          ],
